   "subject": "Do you want to help sustain GGIR?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear GGIR package users,<div><br></div><div>Do you want to know how to help sustain GGIR as an open source research tool?</div><div>Then please read more about the commercial service I have recently set up <a href=\"https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491480390000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02V0xUCuPEP0ey9nl_-nlE\">here</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>Please also share it with your colleagues.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks, Vincent</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "5jlVromcCwAJ",
   "from": "alex.r...@unisa.edu.au",
   "author": "0ba6fa6f78e733b5",
   "date": "2018-02-19T14:26:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: Do you want to help sustain GGIR?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri;color:#141414\">Thanks,\r\nVincent. Great to see this – it is all in our interests to ensure there is\r\ncapacity for GGIR to continue being developed and supported, while the software\r\nitself remains open-source and free.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:#1a1a1a\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri;color:#141414\"> </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:#1a1a1a\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri;color:#141414\">Looking\r\nforward to connecting with yourself and other researchers to discuss\r\npriorities for improvements to the software; I think this will really help\r\ndrive methods forward, while also facilitating comparability between outputs\r\nfrom different studies/surveys.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri;color:#141414\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Calibri;color:#141414\">Alex</span></p>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n</blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "H-1s_guoAAAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "8d92e34685fbc6bd",
   "date": "2018-05-07T21:47:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Re: Do you want to help sustain GGIR?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<div><br></div><div>This is a gentle reminder that if you think that GGIR is valuable for your research then please consider subscribing to my sustainability service: <span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\"><a href=\"https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491480394000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0UWxVVxshwbeahopswMi4y\">https://www.movementdata.nl/how-to-help-sustain-ggir</a>.</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">Needless to say that reporting your issues on<span> </span></span><a href=\"https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/issues\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491480394000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Qt737kAFQ1rYiICxKYo3N\">github</a><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\"><span> </span>or here in the google group is always appreciated, but the efforts needed to help you address them are voluntary.</span><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you are not able to subscribe to the service then consider: actively helping out other GGIR users with questions and issues, contributing to the development of GGIR yourself in person, or getting funding to pay for a scientific programmer to work on GGIR on your behalf.<br></div><div><br></div><div>If you cannot or do not want to commit to either of these options then please understand that I will ignore or at least put a lot less priority on your issues.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks, Vincent</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
